[1mSymbol parity.[22m The C [38;5;10m.so[0m exports four global text symbols — [38;5;10mgotomach[0m, [38;5;10mprocess_value[0m, [38;5;10mdouble_value[0m, [38;5;10mtriple_value[0m. All four are present in [38;5;10mlibgotomach_lib.so[0m, checked two ways: [38;5;10mnm -D --defined-only[0m set difference, and actually resolving each name through [38;5;10mlibloading[0m (which is the stronger claim, since it proves an external caller can reach them). Note the header only declares [38;5;10mgotomach[0m, but the three [38;5;10moperation_fn[0m implementations are non-[38;5;10mstatic[0m in the C, so they are part of the ABI; the translation correctly exports them.[0m[0m
