One thing worth flagging, since it cost a test run: my first version had multiple [38;5;10m#[test][0m functions per binary, and libtest's own [38;5;10mok[0m progress output leaked into the captured fd 1 from a sibling thread, producing a spurious [38;5;10mstdout mismatch[0m on [38;5;10mgotomach(52, 43702, -3, 3702)[0m. That was harness noise, not a divergence. Redirecting fd 1 is process-global, so I consolidated each test binary to a single [38;5;10m#[test][0m entry point and set [38;5;10mRUST_TEST_THREADS=1[0m in the script; if you later split those back into separate [38;5;10m#[test][0m functions, the flakiness will return.[0m[0m
